TI  - [Tracheobronchomalacia in children].
LID - 10.4045/tidsskr.24.0116 [doi]
AB  - This clinical review article aims to describe symptoms and findings in cases of 
      paediatric tracheobronchomalacia to help achieve the correct diagnosis and 
      treatment. Symptoms and signs vary from reduced physical stamina, barking cough, 
      productive cough and gurgling to obstructive episodes or episodes with stridor, 
      which in some cases can be life-threatening. The range of symptoms overlaps with 
      other pulmonary diseases, such as asthma, which increases the risk of 
      misdiagnosis and treatment error. Bronchoscopy is the main diagnostic tool but is 
      resource intensive.
