PG  - 858-862
LID - 10.3760/cma.j.cn112147-20240113-00029 [doi]
AB  - Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) is one of the most common chronic 
      diseases with the highest disease burden in China. In the past, the treatment of 
      COPD was mainly based on drugs. In recent years, interventional bronchoscopy has 
      been tried for the treatment of COPD and some progress has been made. This paper 
      reviewed the clinical application of interventional bronchoscopy for the 
      treatment of COPD to provide information for clinicians.
