TI  - Risk Factors for Procedural Complications of Pediatric Flexible Bronchoscopy: 
      Experience From a Tertiary Care Centre in Northern India.
PG  - 887-889
LID - S097475591600657 [pii]
AB  - We analyzed the records of 869 children who underwent flexible bronchoscopy. We 
      found procedural complications in 6.7% (n = 59), with severe events in 3.2% (n = 
      28). Age < 1 y, recurrent respiratory papillomatosis, and finding lower airway 
      malacia on bronchoscopy were identified as independent risk factors for 
      developing complications with adjusted odds ratio (95% CI) of 2.6 (1.3, 4.9); P = 
      0.004; 5.4 (1.7, 17.6); P = 0.005 and 2.1 (1.1, 4.0); P = 0.031, respectively.
