TI  - [Percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy in a 42-year-old patient with suspected 
      variant of Creutzfeld Jakob disease using a disposable bronchoscope].
PG  - 53-55
LID - 10.1055/a-2406-9419 [doi]
AB  - Prion diseases pose a challenge for flexible reusable endoscopes. Especially for 
      the new variant of Creutzfeld Jakob disease (vCJD) there is currently no suitable 
      processing procedure. In these patients only disposable endoscopes are 
      hygienically safe. The case report shows a PEG placement in a 42-year-old patient 
      with suspected vCJD using a disposable bronchoscope.
