DP  - 2024 Jul
TI  - Bronchoscopic Intervention for Tracheobronchopathia Osteochondroplastica: A 
      Report of Two Cases.
PG  - 3093-3095
LID - 10.1002/lary.31284 [doi]
AB  - Tracheobronchopathia osteochondroplastica (TO) is an uncommon non-malignant 
      tracheal ailment characterized by the existence of numerous bone and/or cartilage 
      nodules in the submucosa of the trachea and bronchi. At present, there is a lack 
      of standardized treatment recommendations for TO. This article presents two 
      instances of severe tracheal stenosis caused by TO, which were effectively 
      managed through the implementation of bronchoscopic stent placement and rigid 
      bronchoscopy curettage, respectively. Both cases exhibited favorable outcomes, 
      providing novel insights and references for the treatment of TO. Laryngoscope, 
      134:3093-3095, 2024.
