VI  - 63
IP  - 15
DP  - 2024 Aug 1
TI  - Overlap of Chronic Pulmonary Aspergillosis on Allergic Bronchopulmonary 
      Aspergillosis.
PG  - 2167-2171
LID - 10.2169/internalmedicine.2562-23 [doi]
AB  - An 80-year-old woman who developed allergic bronchopulmonary aspergillosis (ABPA) 
      was admitted to our institution in 2023 for an enlarged pulmonary mass lesion. 
      She had developed ABPA in 2017, and corticosteroid therapy had improved the 
      mucoid impaction of the bronchi. Because part of the lesion remained, increased 
      doses of corticosteroid, antifungals, and biologics were administered, but the 
      pulmonary lesion enlarged in 2022. Bronchoscopy showed necrotic tissue in the 
      bronchial lumen, and bronchial washing fluid showed neutrophilic inflammation and 
      fungal hyphae. We subsequently diagnosed her as having chronic pulmonary 
      aspergillosis overlapping ABPA, and voriconazole was started that resulted in 
      shrinkage of the nodules.
