TI  - [Surgical or bronchoscopic lung volume reduction for emphysema therapy].
PG  - S51-S70
LID - 10.1055/a-1990-4810 [doi]
AB  - More than 20 years ago, surgical lung volume reduction (LVRS) was already 
      established in patients with advanced emphysema as a palliative therapy option 
      that reduces respiratory distress and improves lung function and quality of life. 
      In addition, bronchoscopic procedures (BLVR) aimed at volume reduction have 
      existed for just over 10 years. The advantages and disadvantages of LVRS and BLVR 
      are discussed in this article.
