TI  - Single Setting Robotic Lung Nodule Diagnosis and Resection.
PG  - 233-244
LID - S1547-4127(23)00039-7 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.thorsurg.2023.04.009 [doi]
AB  - Lung cancer remains the leading cause of cancer-related deaths. Early tissue 
      diagnosis followed by timely therapeutic procedures can have a significant impact 
      on overall survival. While robotic-assisted lung resection is an established 
      therapeutic procedure, robotic-assisted bronchoscopy is a more recent diagnostic 
      procedure that improves reach, stability, and precision in the field of 
      bronchoscopic lung nodule biopsy. The ability to combine lung cancer diagnostics 
      with therapeutic surgical resection into a single-setting anesthesia procedure 
      has the potential to decrease costs, improve patient experiences, and most 
      importantly, reduce delays in cancer care.
