TI  - Intrathoracic tuberculosis: Role of interventional bronchoscopy in diagnosis.
PG  - 23-29
LID - S1526-0542(22)00088-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.prrv.2022.12.002 [doi]
AB  - Tuberculosis (TB) is the leading cause of death from a single infectious agent 
      globally. Mortality is related to the delay in diagnosis and starting treatment. 
      According to new guidelines it is very important to classify pulmonary 
      tuberculosis (PTB) as severe or not severe disease due to the difference in 
      treatment duration. Bronchoscopy is the gold standard for assessing the degree of 
      airway compression and obstruction in paediatric PTB. Paediatric bronchoscopy has 
      evolved from a primarily diagnostic procedure to include interventional 
      bronchoscopy for diagnostic purposes. Endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS) has 
      increased the potential of sampling mediastinal lymph nodes both for histological 
      diagnosis and microbiological confirmation.
