TI  - [Systemic nocardiosis with mediastinal lymph node involvement proven by 
      endoscopic ultrasound].
PG  - 566-570
LID - S0761-8425(22)00208-X [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.rmr.2021.12.012 [doi]
AB  - INTRODUCTION: Systemic nocardiosis is an infectious disease that is rarely 
      associated with mediastinal lymph nodes. CASE REPORT: We report the case of a 
      72-year-old male patient treated with a high dose of oral corticosteroids for 
      rheumatoid polyarthritis. This patient presented with rapid overall deterioration 
      associated with mediastinal lymph nodes. Endobronchial ultrasound enabled us to 
      establish a diagnosis of systemic nocardiosis. The patient recovered after having 
      received suitable antibiotic treatment for four months. CONCLUSION: This work 
      reports on a rare clinical presentation of systemic nocardiosis associated with 
      mediastinal lymphadenopathies and highlights the key role of endobronchial 
      ultrasound in diagnosing mediastinal lymph nodes, especially in differential 
      diagnosis for lung cancer.
