TI  - Foreign body aspiration in two young infants: The devil in the carpet.
PG  - 1795-1798
LID - 10.1002/ppul.25965 [doi]
AB  - Foreign body aspiration is rare in children below 6 months of age. Very young 
      children presenting with stridor, atypical croup presentation, and not responding 
      accordingly, subglottic foreign body aspiration should be considered. These may 
      not always be visible with bedside flexible endoscopy and may need investigation 
      under anesthesia. We report two cases of devil's thorn aspiration in young 
      infants. These children were left on the floor to play and devils thorn may be a 
      danger lurking as the they have been deposited unknowingly by the shoes people 
      wear and pick up by these young infants.
