TI  - A case of exogenous lipoid pneumonia diagnosed by transbronchial lung cryobiopsy.
PG  - 555-558
LID - S2212-5345(21)00033-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.resinv.2021.02.001 [doi]
AB  - A 57-year-old man visited a referral physician due to abnormal chest shadows. 
      Transbronchial lung biopsy (TBLB) failed to diagnose his condition. As 
      antibiotics and systemic steroids did not improve the condition, he was referred 
      to our hospital. A second TBLB in our hospital also failed to diagnose the 
      disease. Transbronchial lung cryobiopsy (TBLC) was performed using radial 
      endobronchial ultrasound with guide sheath (EBUS-GS), and the patient was 
      diagnosed with lipoid pneumonia. Right upper lobe resection was performed, and 
      lipoid pneumonia was confirmed from the surgical specimen. We report a case of 
      lipoid pneumonia diagnosed by EBUS-GS TBLC.
