TI  - [Pleuro-pneumopathy revealing an unusual inhaled bronchial foreign body].
PG  - 297-299
LID - S0761-8425(21)00041-3 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.rmr.2021.01.014 [doi]
AB  - Inhalation of foreign bodies is not often observed in young adults, and may go 
      unnoticed. A 37-year-old patient, with no significant medical history, was 
      admitted for right basal pleuro-pneumopathy. Endoscopic examination revealed the 
      presence of a brittle yellowish formation. It was a bone fragment, accidentally 
      inhaled by the patient. It is necessary to look for an inhaled foreign body in 
      cases of serious infection unusually observed in an immuno-competent patient.
