TI  - [Research Advances in the Diagnostic Value of Rapid On-site Evaluation in 
      Endobronchial Ultrasound-guided Transbronchial Needle Aspiration for Lung 
      Cancer].
PG  - 820-824
LID - 10.3881/j.issn.1000-503X.12183 [doi]
AB  - Rapid on-site evaluation(ROSE),an auxiliary sampling quality evaluation 
      technology,can be used to evaluate the adequacy and diagnostic category of 
      samples,judge the histological type of lung cancer,and optimize the gene type of 
      lung cancer.Applying ROSE to endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial 
      needle aspiration of suspected lung cancer can improve the puncture success rate 
      and diagnostic rate and reduce complications and puncture attempts.Rose performed 
      via remote cytopathology technology or by trained respiratory specialists may 
      become the future trends.
