TI  - Initial experience of virtual-assisted lung mapping utilizing both indocyanine 
      green and indigo carmine.
PG  - 1035-1039
LID - 10.1007/s11748-020-01565-2 [doi]
AB  - Virtual-assisted lung mapping is a bronchoscopic multiple dye marking technique 
      that facilitates sublobar lung resections for unidentifiable pulmonary tumors. 
      Marking failure reportedly occurs in 10% of cases. To overcome this limitation, 
      we developed indocyanine green virtual-assisted lung mapping that uses 
      indocyanine green in addition to indigo carmine. Here, we report our initial 
      experience of indocyanine green virtual-assisted lung mapping.
