TI  - A filamentous trio.
LID - 10.4081/monaldi.2020.1493 [doi]
AB  - Opportunistic infections caused by fungi and unusual bacteria are predominantly 
      encountered in the setting of immunosuppressed host. Co-infections with multiple 
      such organisms can pose multiple challenges even to the astute clinician from 
      establishing the diagnosis to drug interactions during treatment of such 
      infections. We hereby present one such case of a triple opportunistic infection 
      in an immunocompetent host and the difficulties faced in the therapeutic decision 
      making.
