TI  - Antidiarrheal pill in the airway.
PG  - 278-279
LID - 10.5603/ARM.2020.0114 [doi]
AB  - Pill aspiration depicts an unusual type of foreign body aspiration necessitating 
      a discrete diagnostic and therapeutic approach.1 Some pills may remain intact in 
      the endobronchial tree for many years without causing much harm, whereas others 
      may dissolve2 The clinical outcomes may also vary, from an asymptomatic granuloma 
      to severe, life-threatening airway complications, depending upon the chemical 
      properties of the pill. We report a compelling case of pill aspiration in a 
      healthy patient.
