VI  - 68
IP  - 12
DP  - 2020 Dec
TI  - Backtable bronchoplasty for donor tracheal bronchus in lung transplantation.
PG  - 1536-1538
LID - 10.1007/s11748-020-01305-6 [doi]
AB  - The management of a tracheal bronchus in lung transplantation is poorly studied 
      and ill-defined. We report a case of lung transplantation performed using a donor 
      right lung graft with an apical tracheal bronchus and propose a novel anastomosis 
      technique for this procedure. The neo-upper lobe bronchus created by suturing the 
      apical tracheal bronchus and the upper lobe bronchus of the donor was anastomosed 
      to the upper lobe bronchus of the recipient in a double-barrel fashion. A 
      follow-up at 19 months demonstrated no stenosis of the anastomosis. The 
      advantages and potential disadvantages of this procedure are discussed.
