TI  - Bronchoscopical Repair of Tracheal Laceration Using Conventional Instrumentation: 
      A Novel Technique.
PG  - e141-e143
LID - S0003-4975(19)31465-1 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2019.08.074 [doi]
AB  - Postintubation tracheobronchial laceration is a rare complication of endotracheal 
      intubation. It requires early serial treatment in cases of pneumomediastinum with 
      difficulty in ventilation to prevent mediastinitis and stricture. The surgical 
      access to the posterior tracheal wall depends on the site of the laceration. A 
      right posterolateral thoracotomy is performed for lacerations of the 
      middle-distal trachea and a transcervical approach for the upper third. Either of 
      them is associated with specific postoperative morbidities. We describe a novel 
      technique of exclusively intraluminal repair of postintubation tracheobronchial 
      laceration using conventional endoscopic instrumentation through a 14.1-mm rigid 
      bronchoscope.
