TI  - Unusual Presentation of Severe Endobronchial Obstruction Caused by Cryptococcus 
      gattii in a Child.
PG  - 67-70
LID - 10.1093/jpids/piy100 [doi]
AB  - Disease caused by Cryptococcus gattii typically manifests as meningoencephalitis 
      or pulmonary nodules. Endobronchial lesions are rare, and most cases are caused 
      by Cryptococcus neoformans. We describe here a case of endobronchial disease in a 
      child caused by C gattii. The disease spectrum in this patient was notable for 
      the discovery of anti-granulocyte macrophage colony-stimulating factor 
      autoantibodies.
