TI  - Abnormal bronchial origin in the right middle and lower lung.
PG  - 2034-2035
LID - 10.1002/ppul.26996 [doi]
AB  - Congenital anatomical abnormalities of the pediatric bronchus is a rare and 
      easily overlooked condition. In this study, we identified an 8-year-old patient 
      with congenital anomalies of bronchial origin that caused his clinical 
      manifestations of cough and shortness of breath. This diagnosis needs to be taken 
      into possible consideration when similar clinical manifestations occur in a 
      pediatric patient without a cause.
