TI  - [Bronchoscopic management of malignant central airway obstructions].
PG  - 94-100
LID - S0761-8425(22)00455-7 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.rmr.2022.11.084 [doi]
AB  - Up to 30% of lung cancer patients suffer from central airway obstruction, 
      resulting in major deterioration in prognosis and quality of life. Interventional 
      bronchoscopy combines a number of invasive techniques used during rigid 
      bronchoscopy. It is designed to rapidly improve symptoms, primarily dyspnea. 
      Applied according to very precise indications, this technique requires careful 
      patient selection and needs to be incorporated into the multimodal oncological 
      management in combination with systemic treatments, radiation therapy and 
      surgery.
