TI  - Bronchoscopy for removal of foreign body: What's the big deal?
PG  - 592-596
LID - 10.1002/ppul.26226 [doi]
AB  - Foreign bodies of the airway are common occurrences in the pediatric population. 
      Children requiring anesthesia for removal of airway foreign bodies can present 
      many challenges. In this case, the patient required urgent removal of a foreign 
      body while symptomatic with upper and lower respiratory symptoms. Circumstances 
      such as these can result in higher intraoperative and postoperative 
      complications. This presentation describes the clinical decision-making process 
      and the discussion of common modalities for diagnosis, treatment, and anesthetic 
      management.
