DP  - 2022 Jul 27
TI  - Tracheal bronchus: a rare cause of recurrent pneumonia in adults.
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2022-250715 [doi]
LID - e250715
AB  - Tracheal bronchus, also known as bronchus suis, is a rare congenital anomaly of 
      the airway where an accessory bronchus originates directly from the trachea. With 
      an estimated incidence of 0.001%-2.0%, this condition is rarely reported in 
      literature. It is usually discovered as an incidental finding in an otherwise 
      asymptomatic individual. However, it can act as a focus of recurrent infection or 
      present as persistent radiographic infiltrates. Multidetector CT imaging and 
      bronchoscopy play a crucial role in the identification of this entity. We hereby 
      report the case of a middle-aged man who presented with recurrent right upper 
      lobe pneumonia, which was found to be due to an underlying tracheal bronchus.
