TI  - A novel guidewire technique for endobronchial silicone plug occlusion for 
      bronchopleural fistula.
LID - 10.1510/mmcts.2021.063 [doi]
AB  - Successful bronchoscopic bronchopleural fistula closure requires both accurate 
      localization of the fistula and device implantation; placing a silicone plug 
      requires experience and skill because of the limited endobronchial working space. 
      We report a novel bronchoscopic silicone plug placement technique for a 
      bronchopleural fistula that developed after a left upper lobectomy following 
      induction chemoradiation therapy, which was then successfully treated by 
      omentopexy.
