TI  - Endobronchial actinomycosis in a child.
PG  - 3429-3432
LID - 10.1002/ppul.25550 [doi]
AB  - Actinomycosis is a rare, indolent and invasive infection caused by Actinomyces 
      species. Pulmonary actinomycosis is very rarely seen in the paediatric 
      population. The classic radiological presentation of thoracic involvement of 
      actinomycosis includes lower lobe consolidation, empyema and periostitis of the 
      ribs. We report a case of endobronchial actinomycosis in a child diagnosed on 
      endobronchial biopsy and bronchoalveolar lavage (BAL). Bronchoscopy can be 
      dangerous when performed on these cases, as there is a risk of severe bleeding 
      and large airway obstruction, as was the case with this patient.
