TI  - Economic Considerations of Lung Volume Reduction Surgery and Bronchoscopic 
      Valves.
PG  - 211-219
LID - S1547-4127(21)00010-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.thorsurg.2021.02.006 [doi]
AB  - Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease is a challenging disease to treat, and at 
      advanced stages of the disease, procedural interventions become some of the only 
      effective methods for improving quality of life. However, these procedures are 
      often very costly. This article reviews the medical literature on 
      cost-effectiveness of lung volume reduction surgery and bronchoscopic valve 
      placement for lung volume reduction. It discusses the anticipated costs and 
      economic impact in the future as technique is perfected and outcomes are 
      improved.
