TI  - High-Frequency Jet Ventilation for a Patient With Tracheomediastinal Fistula, 
      Tension Pneumomediastinum, and Pneumothorax: A Case Report.
PG  - e01362
LID - 10.1213/XAA.0000000000001362 [doi]
AB  - Tracheomediastinal fistula (TMF) is an uncommon condition and carries a high 
      mortality. We report the anesthetic management of a patient with TMF using stent 
      insertion via rigid bronchoscopy. The TMF was a complication of double-lumen 
      endotracheal tube insertion resulting in a tension pneumomediastinum. Initial 
      intraoperative attempts to ventilate the lungs and overcome the air leak with 
      high gas flow of 45 L/min via the side port of the bronchoscope resulted in a 
      pneumothorax. This case report demonstrates that high-frequency jet ventilation 
      can minimize the air leak and avoid barotrauma during anesthesia for TMF repair.
