LID - 10.1093/icvts/ivaa195 [doi]
AB  - A 71-year-old man had experienced an irritating cough for 3 months. A diagnosis 
      of squamous cell carcinoma in the carina was made from the bronchoscopic 
      examination. The patient underwent a robotic-assisted resection and 
      reconstruction of the carina. The patient's postoperative course was uneventful. 
      This is the first description of the feasibility of robotic-assisted carina 
      resection and reconstruction.
