VI  - 164
DP  - 2020 Sep 3
TI  - [A woman with wheezing].
LID - D4725 [pii]
AB  - A 26-year-old patient experiencing dyspnoea and wheezing during exercise was seen 
      at the outpatient clinic. Asthma was considered, but treatment with salbutamol 
      was unsuccessful. Spirometry revealed plateauing of the inspiratory and 
      expiratory flow-volume loops. CT scan and additional flexible bronchoscopy with 
      dilatation showed circumferential subglottic stenosis. ANA/ANCA tests were 
      negative and biopsy revealed scar tissue with minimal inflammation. Based on 
      these findings, we established a diagnosis of idiopathic subglottic stenosis.
