TI  - Utilization of endobronchial electrocautery for removal of an impacted airway 
      foreign body.
LID - 10.4081/monaldi.2020.1383 [doi]
AB  - Dear Editor, Aspiration of a foreign body into the tracheobronchial tree 
      can occur at any age, though it occurs more commonly in children. In small 
      children, the foreign body commonly gets lodged in the central airways (trachea 
      and mainstem bronchi); hence, the presentation is usually sudden onset of cough 
      and dyspnea or even lifethreatening respiratory failure in an otherwise healthy 
      child. A witnessed aspiration or a history of aspiration can usually be elicited.
