VI  - 29
IP  - 156
DP  - 2020 Jun 30
TI  - Bronchoscopic intratumoural therapies for non-small cell lung cancer.
LID - 10.1183/16000617.0028-2020 [doi]
LID - 200028
AB  - The past decade has brought remarkable improvements in the treatment of non-small 
      cell lung cancer (NSCLC) with novel therapies, such as immune checkpoint 
      inhibitors, although response rates remain suboptimal. Direct intratumoural 
      injection of therapeutic agents via bronchoscopic approaches poses the unique 
      ability to directly target the tumour microenvironment and offers several 
      theoretical advantages over systemic delivery including decreased toxicity. 
      Increases in understanding of the tumour microenvironment and cancer immunology 
      have identified many potential options for intratumoural therapy, especially 
      combination immunotherapies. Herein, we review advances in the development of 
      novel bronchoscopic treatments for NSCLC over the past decade with a focus on the 
      potential of intratumoural immunotherapy alone or in combination with systemic 
      treatments.
