TI  - [Advances of Electromagnetic Navigation Bronchoscopy for Peripheral Pulmonary 
      Lesions].
PG  - 440-445
LID - 10.3779/j.issn.1009-3419.2020.102.04 [doi]
AB  - The incidence of peripheral pulmonary lesions (PPLs) is growing following the 
      adoption of lung cancer screening by low-dose chest CT. The diagnosis and 
      treatment of pulmonary nodules is one of the most difficult problems. Based on 
      the electromagnetic positioning technology, the electromagnetic navigation 
      bronchoscope is guided to the pulmonary nodules for biopsy or treatment, 
      providing a new minimally invasive diagnosis and treatment method for suspicious 
      lung lesions. This paper provides an overview of the current status and progress 
      of electromagnetic navigation bronchoscopy in the diagnosis and treatment of 
      peripheral pulmonary diseases.
