TI  - Novel Bronchoscopic Management of Bronchopleural Fistula Following Pneumonectomy.
PG  - 225-228
LID - sti42/1696 [pii]
LID - 10.52198/23.STI.42.CV1696 [doi]
AB  - Bronchopleural fistula (BPF) is a rare but significant cause of morbidity and 
      mortality in cancer patients undergoing surgical lung resection. The mainstay of 
      treatment for BPF is revision of surgical stump. We describe a case of persistent 
      bronchopleural fistula treated with a novel combination of argon plasma 
      coagulation and fibrin glue.
