TI  - A bronchoscopy-associated pseudo-outbreak of Mycobacterium chelonae and 
      Mycobacterium mucogenicum associated with contaminated ice machine water and ice.
PG  - 2056-2058
LID - 10.1017/ice.2023.101 [doi]
AB  - A pseudo-outbreak of bronchoscopy-associated Mycobacterium chelonae and M. 
      mucogenicum was traced to contaminated ice machine water and ice. A nonsterile 
      ice bath was used to cool uncapped, sterile, saline syringes used to slow 
      procedural bleeding. Joining the growing evidence of bronchoscopy 
      pseudo-outbreaks, our investigation describes several lessons for future 
      prevention.
