DP  - 2023 Feb
TI  - [Endobronchial Hamartoma Treated with Bronchoscopic Microwave Tissue Coagulation 
      and Electrosurgical Snaring:Report of a Case].
PG  - 168-171
AB  - A 35-year-old man had chronic cough and was treated as asthma at local doctor. 
      Since the symptoms was not improved, chest computed tomography( CT) was performed 
      and an approximately 5 mm nodule with calcification was found in the left main 
      bronchi. He was referred to our hospital for treatment. Bronchoscopic examination 
      revealed a polypoid lesion in the membranous part of the left main bronchus. 
      Since transbronchial biopsy revealed no malignant findings, bronchoscopic 
      resection using microwave tissue coagulation and electrosurgical snaring was 
      performed safely under the general anesthesia. The tumor was histologically 
      diagnosed as endobronchial hamartoma.
