TI  - [An Unexpected Complication: Contralateral Tension Pneumothorax following 
      Transbronchial Forceps Biopsy].
PG  - 622-625
LID - 10.1055/a-1775-5693 [doi]
AB  - Ipsilateral pneumothoraces are a common complication after transbronchial forceps 
      biopsy. In this case report, a contralateral tension pneumothorax and a 
      pneumoperitoneum occurred following transbronchial forceps biopsy in addition to 
      an ipsilateral pneumothorax.
