TI  - Bronchoscopic suspect of Herpesvirus infection in critically ill COVID-19 
      patients: two case reports and brief literature review.
PG  - e2021514
LID - 10.23750/abm.v92iS1.12425 [doi]
LID - e2021514
AB  - Herpesviridae infection in COVID-19 patients has been reported, particularly 
      muco-cutaneous lesions. Little is known about Herpesviridae lung infection in 
      critically ill COVID-19 patients. Typical scattered lesions seen through 
      fiberoptic bronchoscopy in these patients should raise the question as to whether 
      to start empirically acyclovir treatment while a Herpesviridae diagnostics result 
      becomes available.
