TI  - [S10 Segmentectomy by Thoracoscopic Surgery for a Bronchial Foreign Body 
      Presenting More than One Year].
PG  - 660-663
AB  - It is often difficult to remove long-standing bronchial foreign bodies by 
      bronchoscopy. A 77-year-old male was referred to our department for removal of a 
      foreign body. Chest computed tomography revealed a nail in the right S10b. A 
      bronchoscopic examination could not detect the nail due to locating beyond the 
      subsegmental tree, so thoracoscopic right S10 segmentectomy was performed. 
      Intraoperative ultrasonography and X-ray fluoroscopy were useful in understanding 
      the margin for resection.
