TI  - Early presentation of post-intubation tracheoesophageal fistula with severe 
      tracheal stenosis in COVID-19 patient.
PG  - e144-e147
LID - 10.1308/rcsann.2020.7065 [doi]
AB  - The current global COVID-19 pandemic is caused by the novel coronavirus severe 
      acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2). Currently, acquired 
      tracheoesophageal fistulas are mainly iatrogenic lesions produced by prolonged 
      tracheal intubation. We present a case of tracheoesophageal fistula with severe 
      tracheal stenosis following tracheal intubation in a patient with SARS-CoV-2 
      infection.
