TI  - Early diagnosis of lung cancer: which is the optimal choice?
PG  - 6214-6227
LID - 10.18632/aging.202504 [doi]
AB  - The prognosis of lung cancer patients with different clinical stages is 
      significantly different. The 5-year survival of stage IA groups can exceed 90%, 
      while patients with stage IV can be less than 10%. Therefore, early diagnosis is 
      extremely important for lung cancer patients. This research focused on various 
      diagnosis methods of early lung cancer, including imaging screening, 
      bronchoscopy, and emerging potential liquid biopsies, as well as volatile organic 
      compounds, autoantibodies, aiming to improve the early diagnosis rate and explore 
      feasible and effective early diagnosis strategies.
