PMC - PMC7377212
OAB - The coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) virus caused a wide spectrum of disease 
      in healthy individuals, as well as those with common comorbidities [1]. Severe 
      COVID-19 is characterised by acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS) secondary 
      to viral pneumonitis, treatment of which may require mechanical ventilation or 
      extracorporeal membrane oxygenation [2]. Clinicians are alert to the possibility 
      of bacterial co-infection as a complication of lower respiratory tract viral 
      infection; for example, a recent review found that 72% of patients with COVID-19 
      received antimicrobial therapy [3]. However, the risk of fungal co-infection, in 
      particular COVID-19 associated pulmonary aspergillosis (CAPA), remains 
      underappreciated.
