TI  - A young male with chronic nonproductive cough diagnosed with blastomycosis in 
      China: a case report.
PG  - 189
LID - 10.1186/s12890-020-01225-4 [doi]
LID - 189
AB  - BACKGROUND: Blastomycosis is a fungal infectious disease prevalent in North 
      America and rarely reported in Asia. Misdiagnosis of malignancy and other 
      infectious diseases were reported. CASE PRESENTATION: A 24-years-old male patient 
      presented with chronic non-productive cough of 4 months duration. He had been 
      diagnosed with Mycobacterium tuberculosis infection and lung malignancy elsewhere 
      and presented to us as the symptoms persisted. We offered him the biopsy under 
      endobronchial ultrasound-guide sheath-transbronchial lung biopsy and sample 
      specimen were sent for next generation sequencing analysis, returned as 
      Blastomyces Dermatitidis infection. The patient was treated by itraconazole for 
      6 months, his symptoms decreased significantly and the CT scan showed resolution 
      of the lesion. CONCLUSION: We shared a case of blastomycosis with delayed and 
      difficult diagnosis and reviewed the knowledge regarding differential diagnosis 
      and next generation sequencing technologies.
