TI  - [Bilateral pneumothorax during awake fiberoptic intubation : A rare complication 
      of bronchoscopy].
PG  - 491-494
LID - 10.1007/s00063-019-0582-7 [doi]
AB  - An 86-year-old woman was scheduled for surgical treatment of a periprosthetic 
      femoral fracture after a fall. Because of a known difficult airway due to 
      multiple surgeries and radiation for cancer in the orofacial area, awake 
      fiberoptic intubation was planned. During the fiberoptic maneuver the patient 
      experienced a massive bout of coughing which resulted in large soft tissue 
      emphysema and double-sided pneumothorax. This case reports a rare complication of 
      fiberoptic intubation and airway management.
