TI  - Antibiotic impregnated cement coated intramedullary nail (ACCIN) using 
      bronchoscopy tubing: technical tips, case series and a review of the literature.
PG  - 683-688
LID - 10.1007/s00590-023-03668-x [doi]
AB  - Antibiotic impregnated cement coated intramedullary nails (ACCINs) have been used 
      in clinical practice for many years and have been shown to help eradicate 
      infection in tibial osteomyelitis while providing stability. We present a novel 
      technique for preparation using bronchoscopy tubing, as well as technical tips 
      and a review of the literature, for ease of preparation and potential subsequent 
      retrieval.
