TI  - Long-standing undiagnosed foreign body aspiration with concomitant pulmonary 
      tuberculosis in an Immunocompetent man.
PG  - 117-118
LID - 10.1177/14782715231161958 [doi]
AB  - Foreign body aspiration is a rare clinical finding in adults, among which very 
      few are reported, probably due to absence of classical clinical features in 
      adults when compared to children and due to lack of awareness. We present a 
      57-year-old with chronic productive cough who was diagnosed to have pulmonary 
      tuberculosis (TB), complicated by long-standing foreign body in the 
      tracheobronchial tree. There are many cases reported in literature where there 
      have been misdiagnosis with respect to pulmonary TB as foreign body or foreign 
      bodies as pulmonary TB. However, this is the first case where retained foreign 
      body and pulmonary TB coexisted in a patient.
