TI  - Robotics in the diagnosis and staging of lung cancer.
PG  - 258-261
LID - 10.1002/jso.27189 [doi]
AB  - The diagnosis of peripheral small lung lesions by electromagnetic navigational 
      bronchoscopy is still inferior to computed tomography (CT) guided percutaneous 
      transthoracic needle lung biopsy. Robotic bronchoscopy is a new technology that 
      may be a potential breakthrough in the diagnosis of small lung lesions. Real-time 
      tools such as electromagnetic navigation, radial-endobronchial ultrasound, and 
      cone beam CT may further improve the diagnostic yield rate may further improve 
      the diagnostic yield rate. In this article, we reviewed early experience of 
      robotic bronchoscopy for diagnosis and staging of lung cancer.
