TI  - Primary Mediastinal Large B-Cell Lymphoma Achieved by Non-Cautery Assisted 
      Transbronchial Mediastinal Cryobiopsy.
PG  - 683-687
LID - 10.1159/000524768 [doi]
AB  - Transbronchial mediastinal cryobiopsy is a novel sampling strategy that shows 
      improved diagnostic utility for mediastinal lesions, particularly in rare tumors 
      and benign disorders, as compared to standard endobronchial ultrasound-guided 
      transbronchial needle aspiration. During this procedure, electrocautery incision 
      is frequently needed to advance the cryoprobe through the airway into the 
      mediastinal lesion, which however results in increased operative difficulty and 
      prolonged procedural time. Here we present a case of mediastinal large B-cell 
      lymphoma successfully diagnosed by transbronchial mediastinal cryobiopsy without 
      cautery-induced airway incision.
