IS  - 0300-5283 (Linking)
VI  - 77
IP  - 2
DP  - 2022 Mar
TI  - Not all wheeze is asthma: A case of central airway foreign body mimicking asthma.
PG  - 246-248
AB  - Foreign body aspirations are more commonly seen in the paediatric age as compared 
      to adults. This is more widely seen in the older population due to the impairment 
      of protective airway mechanisms or the absence of the swallowing reflex, for 
      instance, in neurological diseases, head trauma, alcohol intoxication, sedation, 
      or complications from dental manipulation. We report the case of a betel nut 
      causing airway obstruction in an elderly lady, which was treated multiple times 
      as respiratory tract infection and asthma. Subsequently, a bronchoscopy was 
      performed. Following which, the betel nut was removed causing resolution of 
      symptoms.
