MH  - Tracheostomy/adverse effects/methods/*standards
PMC - PMC7668172
OAB - The current COVID-19 pandemic has rendered up to 15% of patients under mechanical 
      ventilation. Because the subsequent tracheotomy is a frequent procedure, the 
      three societies mostly involved (SEMICYUC, SEDAR and SEORL-CCC) have setup a 
      consensus paper that offers an overview about indications and contraindications 
      of tracheotomy, be it by puncture or open, clarifying its respective advantages 
      and enumerating the ideal conditions under which they should be performed, as 
      well as the necessary steps. Regular and emergency situations are displayed 
      together with the postoperative measures.
