TI  - [Recommendations for Performing Bronchoscopy in Times of the COVID-19 Pandemic].
PG  - 260-262
LID - 10.1055/a-1154-1814 [doi]
AB  - COVID-19, caused by coronavirus SARS-CoV-2 is a new and ongoing infectious 
      disease affecting healthcare systems worldwide. Healthcare worker are at high 
      risk for COIVD-19 and many have been infected or even died in countries severely 
      affected by COVID-19 like China or Italy. Bronchoscopy causes cough and aerosol 
      production and has to be considered a significant risk for the staff to get 
      infected. Particular recommendations should guide to prevent spreading COVID-19 
      and to protect healthcare worker when performing a bronchoscopy.
